  "question": {
    "html": "<p>Monochromatic light of wavelength <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\lambda\"></span> is incident on two slits S<sub>1</sub> and S<sub>2</sub>. An interference pattern is observed on the screen.</p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure></p>\n<p>O is equidistant from S<sub>1</sub> and S<sub>2</sub>. A bright fringe is observed at O and a dark fringe at X.</p>\n<p>There are two dark fringes between O and X. What is the path difference between the light arriving at X from the two slits?</p>\n<p>[1]</p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{\\lambda}{2}\"></span></li><li data-label=\"B\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{3\\lambda}{2}\"></span></li><li data-label=\"C\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{5\\lambda}{2}\"></span></li><li data-label=\"D\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{7\\lambda}{2}\"></span></li></ol>"
  },
